---
import DocShell from '../layouts/doc-shell.astro';
import { docsLinks } from '../lib/nav';
---

<DocShell
   title="WCAG data sources"
   summary="Query bundled WCAG 2.1 and 2.2 criteria, W3C ACT mappings, Quickref tags, and axe-core rule metadata without a network request."
   links={docsLinks}
>
   <section>
      <h2>What ships in the repo</h2>
      <p>
         The <code>packages/wcag-data</code> package syncs structured data from upstream W3C and
         axe-core sources, then generates normalized artifacts that the rest of the toolkit reads
         at runtime.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2>Upstream sources</h2>
      <ul>
         <li>W3C WCAG 2.1 and 2.2 JSON: criteria, levels, normative text, techniques, and failures</li>
         <li>W3C ACT mapping: machine-readable rule-to-criterion coverage</li>
         <li>W3C Quickref tags: topic tags keyed by success criterion</li>
         <li>The installed axe-core package: rule IDs, tags, and ACT rule IDs</li>
      </ul>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2>Choose a test from the coverage result</h2>
      <ol>
         <li>Resolve the WCAG version (default: 2.2) before running any checks.</li>
         <li>Look up the criterion or target level before opening a browser.</li>
         <li>Check coverage and testing strategy to know what can be automated.</li>
      </ol>
   </section>

   <section class="field-note">
      <h2>Coverage limits</h2>
      <p>
         Bundled WCAG data makes criterion lookup local. Some criteria map to axe rules, some need
         screen reader output, and some require human review. The
         <code>wcag coverage</code> command shows which category each criterion falls into.
      </p>
   </section>
</DocShell>
